Package: claude-broker
Version: @VERSION@
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.12)
Recommends: systemd
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://github.com/benstaniford/claude-broker
Description: Claude Code as a local service for containers
 Runs `claude -p` as the user who installed it, with their Claude login,
 and serves client apps (usually Docker containers) over one unix socket
 each. Apps send prompts, JSON schemas and text-only profiles; replies
 stream back as NDJSON. Runs are locked down: only the folders and tools a
 client is configured for, no user settings, hooks or MCP servers. An app's
 own tools are an MCP server inside its container, relayed by the broker,
 so no client code runs on the host.
 .
 Needs Claude Code installed and logged in for that user. After installing:
 claude-broker setup
